&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Related Reference:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
Zaneveld, J.R., D.E. Burkepile, A.A. Shantz, C. Pritchard, R. McMinds, J. Payet, R. Welsh, A.M.S. Correa, N.P. Lemoine, S. Rosales, C.E. Fuchs, and R. Vega Thurber (2016) Overfishing, nutrient pollution, and temperature interact to disrupt coral reefs down to microbial scales. Nature Communications 7:11833 &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.nature.com/articles/ncomms11833&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;doi:10.1038/ncomms11833&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.nature.com/articles/ncomms11833#supplementary-information&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Supplementary Information&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Processing Description:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;p&gt;This dataset contains parrotfish bite observations for the study plots at Pickles Reef, Florida Keys National Marine Sanctuary from 2009-2013.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;u&gt;Natural history of the study site:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
